tps://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-beta/rev/f88f6b3bde9e†hg.mozilla.org L832: \nL833: cite178†Image†bugzilla.mozilla.org L834: \nL835: cite42† Emilio Cobos Álvarez [:emilio] L836: \nL837: Assignee\nL838: ###  cite136†Comment 19 L839: \nL840: •\nL841: \nL842: 29 days ago\nL843: \nL844: Attached file cite72† Bug 2013337 - Fix missing-closing-characters checks in custom property parsing. — cite73†Details L845: \nL846: What is going on in this page is:\nL847: \nL848:   * We have two nested references + fallback, both with missing closing\nL849: parens.\nL850:   * But the value actually ends with a closing paren, the rgb() function.\nL851: So we fail to detect that the closing parens are missing, and we mess up\nL852: the indices during substitution because we rely on the fallback end\nL853: being the end of the var() reference minus 1.\nL854: \nL855: Properly tests for it by checking the block end against the\nL856: outside-of-the-block start. If they're the same there was no closing\nL857: paren. We could extend cssparser with this information maybe but for now\nL858: this seems ok. UnquotedUrl I think we can leave as-is.\nL859: Add two tests, once with a would be successful substitution that we get\nL860: wrong right now, but this patch fixes, and the actually crashing test.\nL861: \nL862: I'm a bit surprised that no fuzzer has found this before tbh...\nL863: \nL864: Original Revision: cite137†https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D281506†phabricator.services.mozilla.com L865: \nL866: cite179†Image†bugzilla.mozilla.org L867: \nL868: cite97† Phabricator Automation L869: ###  cite138†Updated L870: \nL871: •\nL872: \nL873: 29 days ago\nL874: \nL875: cite73†Attachment #9542323 - Flags: approval-mozilla-esr140?\nL876: \nL877: cite180†Image†bugzilla.mozilla.org L878: \nL879: cite97† Phabricator Automation L880: \nL881: ###  cite139†Comment 20 L882: \nL883: •\nL884: \nL885: 29 days ago\nL886: ### firefox-esr140 Uplift Approval Re